PURPOSE
=======
None of the export modules archives the mail packets they generate.
This program will archive the mail, put it in the user's directory,
and update the last read pointers.

Why doesn't the export modules do this, you might ask? We make this
package first and foremost for our own needs. One of these needs
are to be compatible with ABBS. ABBS has a scratchpad where the
export command place mail, and it doesn't archive the mail before
the user asks it to.


REQUIREMENTS
============
Pack needs:
   ...Zeus to be running.
   ...Phoenix's config file.
   ...the user to have a configuration defined.
   ...Files.tmp in the work path (Generated by the export modules).
   ...Delete to be in C:.


USAGE
=====
Pack uses dos.library's ReadArgs(). The template looks like this:

   USER/A,ARCQUIET=AQ/S,ERRORQUIET=EQ/S,SETRC=RC/S

Where:
   User       -> The user's name.
   ArcQuiet   -> Don't output the archiving.
   ErrorQuiet -> Don't print error messages/codes.
   SetRc      -> Set a local variable telling how it went.

For more information about "SetRc" see the section below about
error codes.


RESULT
======
If everything goes as planned Pack will archive the packet, and
place it the user's directory. The name of the archive depends
on what packet format it is and how many waiting packets there
are:

QWK:
<BBS Id>.QWK
<BBS Id><Packet number>.QWK

BLUEWAVE:
<BBS Id>.<A three digit packet number>

MBBS:
<BBS Id>.<Archiver's suffix>
<BBS Id><Packet number>.<Archiver's suffix>


ERROR
=====
These are the error codes/messages:

RC | Error message
===+==================================================================
 0 | -None (Everything should be ok)-
 1 | Wrong arguments
 2 | Can't open zeus.library
 3 | Can't open pipeutil.library
 4 | Can't get shared data (Is Zeus running?)
 5 | Can't load the user
 6 | Can't load user's XData
 7 | Can't load user's Phoenix configuration
 8 | Can't load Phoenix's configuration
 9 | Can't find files to archive
10 | -This code isn't in use-
11 | Can't find which files to archive
12 | Too many waiting mail packets
13 | Illegal archiver number (Change it)
14 | Can't find which files to archive
15 | Out of memory
16 | Error in compress string (Tell the sysop)
17 | Packet aborted
18 | Error archiving files
19 | Can't delete files
===+==================================================================

If you have specified "ErrorQuiet" the error messages should
never be printed. However this isn't true for RC 1 since Pack
didn't manage to parse the arguments.

If you have specified "SetRc" Pack will set a global ENV variable
called "PnxPackErr.<user name>", which contains the return code. You
can fetch this variable from Arexx with Zeus's GetVar().

A little note about RC 0: It's true what the error message says.
It should never happend, because RC 0 isn't an error. However the
"PnxPackErr" variable will be set.
